    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20497" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Herbĭta</span></b> , ae,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑρβίτα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in Sicily</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 3, 32, §
			75</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Deriv. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Herbĭtensis</span></b> ,
				e, adj., <i>of</i> or
				<i>belonging to Herbita</i>, <i>Herbitan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 3, 18, § 47</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Herbĭtenses</span></b> ,
			ĭum, m.
			plur., <i>the inhabitants of
			Herbita</i>, <i>Herbitans</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 2, 65, §
		156</span></i>.</div>
